Chapter: RandomGetRefusal
  cites Foreword chapter Random
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A failed random_get writes nothing, so a lowering that ignores its errno reads whatever lies at the heap pointer;
 fresh memory reads 0, which the wrapper already refuses. The stale words left by a released allocation make the
 two lowerings answer differently.

  verdict : Maybe (List Integer) -> Text
  verdict (m) = when m
    is None -> "refused"
    is Just (ws) -> "drawn " & show (list-length ws)

  stale : Integer -> Integer
  stale (n) = let mark = __heap-save
    in let junk = [n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n, n]
    in let size = list-length junk
    in let gone = __heap-restore mark
    in size

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let s = stale 12345
    in print-line-uni ("hardware-random-words: " & verdict (hardware-random-words 2))
  end